        "original_id": "d113625a-3f1d-5220-ba64-ac6f3127b939",
        "text": "This chunk is about:\n- People: Damian Green\n- Topics: Parliamentary privilege in the United Kingdom, MPs expenses scandal, super-injunctions\n- Events: 2010 MPs expenses scandal, arrest of Damian Green\n- Cases: RJW & SJW v The Guardian newspaper & Person or Persons Unknown, CTB v News Group Newspapers\n- Roles: Member of Parliament for Ashford, First Secretary of State, Minister for the Cabinet Office\n\nFacts:\n- In 2010, the doctrine of Parliamentary privilege in the United Kingdom was unsuccessfully used to try to prevent details of the 2010 MPs expenses scandal from emerging.\n- In recent years, the doctrine of Parliamentary privilege in the United Kingdom made headlines in relation to the arrest of Damian Green.\n- In recent years, the doctrine of Parliamentary privilege in the United Kingdom also made headlines in relation to super-injunction cases including RJW & SJW v The Guardian newspaper & Person or Persons Unknown, known as Trafigura, and CTB v News Group Newspapers.\n- The recent headlines about Parliamentary privilege in the United Kingdom led to calls to reform the law relating to privilege.\n- Damian Howard Green was born on 17 January 1956.\n- Damian Green has been the Conservative Member of Parliament for Ashford since 1997.\n- Damian Green has served as First Secretary of State and Minister for the Cabinet Office since 11 June 2017.",
        "type": "TextSummary"
      },
      {
        "id": 1,
